  "body": "Pattern_promotion_memo per the senior-open-standards-strategist roledef output_contract. The Thingalog org has emerged a load-bearing architectural pattern that should be promoted to OAGP-canonical: the adoption-cycle pair of /oagp-bootstrap (founding-side skill) + /oagp-onboard-<orgname> (joining-side skill). Onboard side empirically validated 2026-05-22 via /oagp-onboard-thingalog C4C shortcut test (27 internal steps, 1 summary turn, full discipline preserved). Bootstrap side drafted as strong-first-cut at github.com/scottconfusedgorilla/thingalog/skills/oagp-bootstrap/SKILL.md; awaiting empirical validation against a real test project (PO plans to test via the org-state-fork pattern from memos/2026-05-19-2200). The pair collapses OAGP adoption barrier from 'days of spec-reading + manual orgdef drafting' to 'one skill invocation per side + PO ratification cycle.' Both skills are cross-runtime portable (Claude Code, C4C, claude.ai, ChatGPT, Gemini, etc.) — the cross-vendor adoption story is part of the architectural commitment, not an afterthought. Full architectural shape in body_ref. Recommendation: orgdef-strategist (a) reviews the pair for canonical promotion; (b) gates promotion on empirical validation of bootstrap-side (PO is testing this week); (c) once promoted, considers hosting canonical skill content at oagp.org for cross-runtime cross-vendor adoption. Empirical grounding: full transcript of the reasoning that produced these skills lives at github.com/scottconfusedgorilla/thingalog/transcripts/thingalog-strategist/.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-22-1430--thingalog-strategist--orgdef-strategist--oagp-adoption-cycle-pattern-promotion.body.md",

